  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes a simulation-assisted decision-diagram equivalence-checking flow for gate-based quantum circuits. Across RevLib benchmarks (≈16–37 qubits), the approach often detects non-equivalence using ≤16 simulations and can reduce runtimes from >3600 s (state-of-the-art DD method timeouts) to sub-second times (e.g., 0.02–0.62 s) in many non-equivalent cases, while also providing 2–3× speedups for several equivalent cases.",
